# Flutter / Dart
**/.dart_tool/
**/.packages
**/build/
# Every lockfile is committed, and all of them must be generated with the SDK
# pinned in .fvmrc.
#
# "Library packages stay unpinned" is a convention for *published* libraries,
# where the lockfile is meaningless to whoever depends on you. These five are
# `publish_to: none` members of one monorepo that is only ever built as a
# whole, so the convention does not apply — and leaving four of them unpinned
# meant they resolved fresh on every clone and every CI run. A dependency
# publishing a bad patch release turned the build red with no commit in the
# repository that caused it, and nothing to bisect.
#
# A pub workspace would additionally unify the five resolutions, and is not an
# option here — see the note in the Makefile.
apps/client/android/.gradle/
apps/client/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
apps/client/.flutter-plugins
apps/client/.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Node / Backend
node_modules/
dist/
apps/backend/dist/

# Cloudflare Worker (apps/feedback-worker)
.wrangler/
apps/feedback-worker/.dev.vars
npm-debug.log*

# Env
.env
apps/backend/.env

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
